hich would represent tool-authored metadata more honestly. The documentation is inconclusive about whether those records are passed to the model during resume or merely used by the CLI/UI.\n\nThe probe would fabricate tiny sessions containing unique markers in:\n\n- a user message;\n- a `system` record;\n- an `attachment` record;\n\nThen resume each and ask Claude to report which markers it can see.\n\nPossible outcomes:\n\n- If `system` reaches context, use it for the notice.\n- Otherwise, if `attachment` reaches context, use that.\n- If neither does, retain the synthetic user message because correctness outweighs the role-label imperfection.\n\nIt is non-urgent because the current notice works and is clearly labeled as turnbridge-authored. This would only improve how faithfully Claude represents its role. It requires actual Claude model calls, so I left it as an explicit empirical TODO rather than guessing.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0f25b10d04d81a7e016ab5bbb94dbc87d2be136ebf4818b894","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"],"create_time":1790294966.209103,"turn_id":"01a0d5e5-37b9-73b3-b733-f0c2a2c660df"},"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"don't currently have a claude subscription and they have no free trials so we'll have to leave this as a todo for after all the other CLIs are supported and i make api keys for each of them for minimal support testing","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0d5fa-17c9-7a23-9aac-1816548723e8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1790296332.23348,"turn_id":"01a0d5fa-17a9-7db3-b305-d47342428ab1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Agreed. Leave it deferred until the broader cross-CLI support-testing phase, when provider API keys are available.\n\nIt is already isolated in `docs/TODO_HANDOFF.md` as a non-blocking investigation. No current behavior or release work depends o