{"content":{"activity_type":"event_msg/task_complete","completed_at":1790294977,"duration_ms":13144,"last_agent_message":"It’s a small Claude Code format experiment:\n\n> Can turnbridge store its import notice as a native Claude `system` or `attachment` record while still ensuring the resumed model receives it?\n\nToday, Claude imports the notice as a synthetic user message:\n\n```text\n[turnbridge import notice] This conversation was imported from …\n```\n\nThat reliably reaches model context, but falsely looks like something the user said. Claude session files also support `system` and `attachment` records, which would represent tool-authored metadata more honestly. The documentation is inconclusive about whether those records are passed to the model during resume or merely used by the CLI/UI.\n\nThe probe would fabricate tiny sessions containing unique markers in:\n\n- a user message;\n- a `system` record;\n- an `attachment` record;\n\nThen resume each and ask Claude to report which markers it can see.\n\nPossible outcomes:\n\n- If `system` reaches context, use it for the notice.\n- Otherwise, if `attachment` reaches context, use that.\n- If neither does, retain the synthetic user message because correctness outweighs the role-label imperfection.\n\nIt is non-urgent because the current notice works and is clearly labeled as turnbridge-authored. This would only improve how faithfully Claude represents its role. It requires actual Claude model calls, so I left it as an explicit empirical TODO rather than guessing.","started_at":1790294964,"time_to_first_token_ms":5168,"turn_id":"01a0d5e5-37b9-73b3-b733-f0c2a2c660df"},"context":{"branch":"main","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/turnbridge","head":"502e299c790298f777d34ed6cb1646b57c718e22","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/turnbridge.git"},"id":"ev2-30986b9a72a1470aa92940b11ebec0a31123fed83562b215534efb67bedcdd53","kind":"activity","meta":{"actor":{"type":"agent"},"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","provider":"openai",